 @dualpapayas  almost any GPUs, iGPU, APU from 2014 or newer, can handle AV1 and VP9 playback by default.

There are 2 main reason; AVX2 just came out publicly, and SSE4 SSE4.1 SSE4.2 SSE4.A just got updated. All these happened in 2014. Those are mandatory for OpenCL hardware acceleration.

That's why Core i7 4790k iGPU which is IntelHD 4400 can play AV1 & VP9. But Core i7 3770K iGPU can't. Same thing with GeForce GTX 7 series and newer.
